Looking at the graph, the function h begins at the closed point (-5, 4) on the left and ends at the closed point (4, -5) on the right. The curve is continuous between these endpoints, passing through (-3, 3), (0, 7), and (3, 1).

The domain consists of all x-values covered by the graph: from x = -5 to x = 4, inclusive.

